A first cell
A cell holds PHP without an opening &lt;?php tag. Whatever the cell prints with echo appears first, and the value of its last expression appears after it.

$primes = [2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13];

echo count($primes), " primes, summing to ", array_sum($primes), "\n";

array_sum($primes) / count($primes);

6 primes, summing to 41


6.833333333333333


A cell whose last expression is a statement or a call that returns null shows only what it printed.

State between cells
Variables, objects, functions, and classes carry from one cell to the next.

$primes[] = 17;

$primes;

[2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17]


Restarting the kernel starts a new PHP session with nothing defined. In JupyterLab, use Kernel &gt; Restart Kernel. Each quarto render starts a new session.

Rich output
A phibble data frame is shown as a table and a phiz plot as a chart. The kernel sends each value in every format it can produce, and the front end picks one. Output formats lists which one each Quarto format uses.
Any class can provide its own output:

toHtml(): string supplies HTML.
toMimeBundle(): array supplies several formats at once, keyed by MIME type.


final class Progress
{
    public function __construct(private readonly int $done, private readonly int $total) {}

    public function toHtml(): string
    {
        return sprintf(
            '&lt;progress value="%d" max="%d"&gt;&lt;/progress&gt; %d of %d',
            $this-&gt;done,
            $this-&gt;total,
            $this-&gt;done,
            $this-&gt;total,
        );
    }

    public function __toString(): string
    {
        return sprintf('%d of %d', $this-&gt;done, $this-&gt;total);
    }
}

new Progress(7, 9);

 7 of 9


Juphyter\display() shows a value part way through a cell, so one cell can show several tables or plots.

Juphyter\display(new Progress(3, 9));
Juphyter\display(new Progress(9, 9));

 3 of 9


 9 of 9
